<p>Before I begin, I would like to thank both you and Petrograd for your feedback on the article. I appreciate it when more experienced users are able to notice and point out where my articles clear shortcomings are. I'm going to address both your post and petrograd's here as many of your points overlap.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Show&nbsp;response&nbsp;to&nbsp;criticism</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hide&nbsp;response&nbsp;to&nbsp;criticism</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So there are several things in both your feedback and petrograds that I notice and admit I may have fallen short on in terms of the writing of this article. The primary thing that you both address is the connection between the SCP and Mr. Adachi. Mr Adachi is physically linked to the prions spatially in a similar way to what was going on with 2378, except as you've pointed out 2431 is sentient/weakly sapient, and when shown Mr. Adachi in his current deteriorating state in addition to a portion of his children's book referring to Japanese Mythology, the prions begin to make cranes in an attempt to appeal to the god of longevity so that they might save their inadvertent creator. I attempted to drop significant narrative hints throughout the piece, but obviously some of those have been missed and the hints that were picked up on weren't enough to connect the whole story. I will need to go back to my sandbox and make the connections more solid.</p>
<p>Addendum 1 is primarily there as an explanation for those actually interested in the molecular and biochemical aspects of the prion. This issue is easily fixed, and I can clarify in article and arrange the comment so that it is not as immersion breaking.</p>
<p>The Pseudo Science not making sense is a result of poor wording on my part, Each new protein also spontaneously doubles every 2 weeks, I will fix that in the actual article and my sandbox.</p>
<p>Both you and Petrograd pointed out the emotional indicators, and I can easily rectify this in the experiment section, and also redress your concern about the Foundation recognizing it as being smarter than most domestic animals involving testing for further emotional recognition and quantification.</p>
<p>In regards to your last point Psul, the purpose of the last addenda is primarily to show the failure of the prions attempts to cure Mr. Adachi of Creutzfeld-Jakobs disease and his slow spiral downwards as his physical and mental health continue to degrade. Like most Neurodegenerative disorders and Prion diseases, CJD results in weakened lung function over time. This leaves persons susceptible to pneumonia and other respiratory infections. I primarly left the end result vague to let the reader draw an interpretation of what is going on, however in light of your feed back I may need to make the link more direct.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>To summarise, Psul and Petrograd I will make some major edits in my sandbox and transfer them back over here. Hopefully these edits will make the narrative more clear, and alleviate some of the issues you are experiencing while reading the article.</p>
<p>Edit: I am actually going to change the dobuling time of the protein to be more reasonable with what might be observed of a microscopic organism.</p>

